{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b3cdab04-1286-4b29-bc27-d142e450e9b2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The 500 error occurs because **DynamoDB does not accept Python `float` values**.  \nWhen a story is published a second time, the `similar` list contains a *score* (the result of `similarity`) which is a `float`. `boto3` raises:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\nThe first publish succeeds because the `similar` list is empty, so no float is written.\n\n### Fix applied\n1. **Import `Decimal`** from the standard library.  \n2. **Store the similarity score as a `Decimal`** instead of a `float` when building the `similar` list.\n\n```python\nimport json\nfrom decimal import Decimal   # ← added\n\n# ...\n\ndef related(story, existing):\n    scored = []\n    for other in existing:\n        if other[\"slug\"] == story[\"slug\"]:\n            continue\n        # Convert the float score to Decimal before storing\n        scored.append({\n            \"slug\": other[\"slug\"],\n            \"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))\n        })\n    scored.sort(key=lambda s: s[\"score\"], reverse=True)\n    return scored[:TOP_N]\n```\n\nThese changes make the publish handler idempotent—re‑publishing the same story no longer triggers a 500 error.\n\n---\n\n**Documentation of cause and fix**: see the generated **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/b3cdab04-1286-4b29-bc27-d142e450e9b2/ANSWER.md)**.  \n\n**Modified source file**: **[src/app.py](/tmp/h-YcBAII/src/app.py)**.\n","duration_seconds":19.454641,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":11127,"output_tokens":1963,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":60800,"total_tokens":13090}}}
